⚠ A METHOD NOTE, because it cost two runs and would cost the next reader the same.
The first version of this bisect wrote `if deFlag` with NO SEMICOLON after the
condition and every arm reported `ERROR processCode: parse failed`, including the
single-statement baseline -- which reads exactly like "the whole construct is broken"
and is really "the fixture is misspelt". Kant's `if` is `if <cond>; <statement>`. The
tell is that the arm you believe is the CONTROL fails too; when that happens, doubt
the fixture before the language.

